`getClusterTitleWidth` is a synchronous function but `createLabel` is `async`. `label` will be a `Promise` object, not a DOM element. The next line `label.getBBox().width` will throw `TypeError: label.getBBox is not a function`, and `elem.node().removeChild(label)` will also fail.

Fix: make the function `async` and `await` the call:
```js
export const getClusterTitleWidth = async (elem, node) => {
  const label = await createLabel(elem, node.label, node.labelStyle, undefined, true);
  ...
};
```
This was the original (correct) behaviour in `dagre-wrapper/clusters.js` and the parallel `async`/`await` pattern should be applied here too.

In the `startLabelRight` block, `createLabel` is called with `startEdgeLabelRight` (the outer `g.edgeTerminals`) as the parent, but then the label is immediately reparented to `inner` via `inner.node().appendChild(startLabelElement)`. This is inconsistent with the three other terminal-label blocks in this same function (`startLabelLeft`, `endLabelLeft`, `endLabelRight`), all of which correctly pass `inner` as the parent directly.

The current code works only because a DOM `appendChild` on an already-attached node silently moves it, but it leaves the label transiently attached to the wrong container. The fix is to pass `inner` consistently:
```js
const startLabelElement = await createLabel(
  inner,  // not startEdgeLabelRight
  edge.startLabelRight,
  getLabelStyles(edge.labelStyle)
);
```
The same issue exists at the corresponding location in `packages/mermaid/src/dagre-wrapper/edges.js`.

Same `startLabelRight` bug as in `rendering-util/rendering-elements/edges.js`: `createLabel` receives `startEdgeLabelRight` (the outer container) instead of `inner`. The label is then moved to `inner` by `inner.node().appendChild(startLabelElement)` on the following line, but the other three terminal-label blocks all pass `inner` directly. Pass `inner` here for consistency and to avoid the unnecessary intermediate DOM attachment:
```js
const startLabelElement = await createLabel(
  inner,  // not startEdgeLabelRight
  edge.startLabelRight,
  edge.labelStyle
);
```
